{
  "file": "crates/trust-but-verify/src/agent/project_sources.rs",
  "item": "mod[tests]/impl[Project/Domain]/fn[node_path]",
  "citations": [
    {
      "role": "cite",
      "name": "habeas:coverage",
      "commentary": "Source-tool tests publish OutlineData addresses and retain mapped NodeIds\n directly in dependencies. This required Domain method is unused in\n those flows; stable-path and filesystem-storage tests use other domains."
    }
  ],
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The `habeas:coverage` citation on `crates/trust-but-verify/src/agent/project_sources.rs#mod[tests]/impl[Project/Domain]/fn[node_path]` is acceptable. It is a substantive reason that agrees with the current source, and it sits in fenced commentary on an explicit function with a body, which is the form the built-in requires.\n\n- **Why the method exists:** `node_path` is a required `Domain` trait method. The test fixture `Project` has to implement it.\n- **What the project-source tests use:** They exercise `ReadSource`, `refresh_evidence` and the source tools. Their dependencies are only `Dependency::Node(...)` values. An example is `deterministic_source_reads_reuse_saved_results`. The fixture's `outgoing_edges` always returns an empty vector, so no `OutgoingEdges` dependency is recorded. `Project`'s `load_evidence` and `store_evidence` ignore the node and criterion arguments and use an in-memory record, so they never call `node_path`.\n- **Where `node_path` is called elsewhere:** A search found its only non-test caller to be `edge_fingerprint` in `graph.rs`. That function runs for `OutgoingEdges` dependencies, through `prepare_edges` and `dependencies_are_current`. Neither runs here, which supports the claim that the method is unused in these flows.\n- **The other domains:** The path-stability and storage tests use other domains. Examples are `Application` in `tests/contracts.rs` and `StoredGraph` in `tests/support/stored_graph.rs`. The latter's `load_evidence` and `store_evidence` call `node_path`. This matches the comment's reference to stable-path and filesystem-storage tests.\n\nThe justification is that the method is required but unused by this fixture's flows, not that it is hard to cover, so it is more than difficulty alone. I found no gap.",
